          "question_type": "cefr_listen_detail",
          "rubric": null,
          "sample_answer": null,
          "script": "Man: You spent ten years in banking before becoming a teacher. What made you change?\nWoman: People assume it was the money or the stress – and the hours were long, I won't deny it. But what really decided it was a volunteering scheme my bank ran. I spent a few afternoons helping teenagers with maths, and I realised I looked forward to those afternoons more than anything in my actual job.",
