            "passage": "Dear Editor,\nI read with interest your report on the council's plan to close the city centre to private cars from next spring. As someone who cycles to work every day, I ought to be delighted, and in principle I am. Cleaner air and quieter streets would benefit everyone.\nMy concern is with the timing. The new tram line, which the council itself describes as essential to the scheme, will not be finished until at least the following year. Until then, people who live outside the city and cannot cycle – including many older residents and shift workers – will have no reliable way to get in. Local shops, many of which are still recovering from a difficult few years, could lose customers they simply cannot afford to lose.\nI would urge the council to delay the ban until the trams are running, rather than abandon it altogether. A good idea introduced too early can easily turn people against it.\nYours faithfully,\nHelen Brooks",
