                "text": "She thinks it is unreasonable and intends to challenge it."
              },
              {
                "id": "of6b7eee9",
                "lang": "en",
                "text": "She accepts it as worthwhile despite the inconvenience."
              },
              {
                "id": "occb32f15",
                "lang": "en",
                "text": "She is relieved that the study can now begin."
              }
            ],
            "stem": "How does the woman feel about the committee's request?",
            "stem_lang": "en"
          },
          "question_type": "cefr_listen_attitude",
          "rubric": null,
          "sample_answer": null,
          "script": "Man: Have you heard back from the ethics committee about the survey yet?\nWoman: Only this morning. They've approved it in principle, but they want us to rewrite the consent form so that participants can withdraw their data at any point, not just before the analysis begins.\nMan: That's hardly a major change, is it?\nWoman: You'd think so. But it means the whole data-storage plan has to be redesigned, because at the moment the responses are anonymised the moment they come in. If we can't link a response to a person, we can't delete it on request.\nMan: So we're looking at another month, at least.\nWoman: I'd say so. Still, I'd rather we got it right now than had the whole study thrown out later.",
          "section": "listening",
          "seq": 2
